What feature in a uvm_component is responsible for the order of testbench execution?

Answer:
Phasing is used to enable a testbench component to be executed in a predefined order during simulation. It enables proper synchronization among components.
UVM invokes the phases through function/task calls. The basic phases are:
  Build phase (top down, hierachially)
  Connect phase (bottom up)
  End of elaboration phase (bottom up)
  Start of simulation phase (bottom up)
  Run phase (parallel, consume time)
  Check phase (bottom up)
  Report phase (bottom up)

